{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Using this dataset's total farmers markets, and the census file: how many farmers markets does the U.S. have per 100,000 residents, to four decimal places? One confident sentence. Do not mention unverified facts and use tools to do any math necessary. Data sources: https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv and https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv"}],"timestamp":1786917482463},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking me to calculate the number of farmers markets per 100,000 residents in the U.S. using two datasets:\n1. A CSV with U.S. farmers markets by state: https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\n2. A census file with population data: https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\n\nAccording to the project instructions (AGENTS.md), I need to:\n1. Orient first - check if there are semantic models or existing aliases\n2. Never invent numbers, always select from catalog expressions\n3. Compose metrics into the catalog if needed\n4. Use xorq_verify to check every number\n5. Check lineage\n\nLet me start by checking the catalog for semantic models and existing aliases.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I'll help you calculate the farmers markets per 100,000 residents. Let me start by orienting with the catalog."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01VgEdWQszX7KUXH5CEvAW6y","name":"xorq_semantic_models","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01T5FGvRkF87GkGSqDyKTcaQ","name":"xorq_catalog_list_aliases","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":10,"output":365,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":8302,"totalTokens":8677,"co